  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.084,
            0.609,
            0.125
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Observe whether water seeps through to the other side of the plate or not."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.128,
            0.58,
            0.169
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Keep observing this at regular intervals until the water completely disappears."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.17,
            0.573,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What do you infer? Is this activity enough to come to the conclusion that water does not seep through a steel plate?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.232,
            0.583,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If water does not seep through the steel plate. Then, where has the water gone?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.617,
            0.08,
            0.91,
            0.291
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.617,
                0.08,
                0.91,
                0.291
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_2_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.273,
            0.63,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This water gets converted into gaseous state called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "water vapour",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". The water vapour is another state of water. Let us think of another observation where you notice the water disappearing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.667,
            0.305,
            0.86,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 8.1: Steel plate with a tablespoon of water"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.372,
            0.605,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "While making dosa, we sprinkle some water on the hot pan and it disappears. Where does it go?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.277,
            0.441,
            0.416,
            0.461
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us draw"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.469,
            0.543,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Draw a detailed sketch (with labels and caption) about what happens to the water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.573,
            0.375,
            0.701,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.573,
                0.375,
                0.701,
                0.564
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_2_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.524,
            0.565,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The water which is sprinkled on the hot pan gets converted into steam. Steam is actually water vapour, some part of which converts into water droplets."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.699,
            0.407,
            0.875,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Water vapour is actually invisible but the presence of tiny droplets of water in the steam makes it visible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.6,
            0.575,
            0.689,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you know?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.611,
            0.565,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The process of conversion of water into its vapour state is called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "evaporation",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.655,
            0.743,
            0.719
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The process of evaporation takes place continuously, even at room temperature. Can you think of other examples of evaporation?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.72,
            0.742,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Drying of wet clothes, mopped floor, and sweat on our body are some examples of it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.763,
            0.744,
            0.849
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now what do you think is the reason for the disappearance of water from the puddles? Is it due to: (i) seeping of water into the ground or (ii) evaporation of water or (iii) both of these?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.85,
            0.742,
            0.894
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hand sanitiser disappears as you rub it on your hands. What happens to it?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.889,
            0.698,
            0.908,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Journey through States of Water"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 20,
